Make the output and the consumed offsets one Kafka transaction. Consumer: group.id=enricher, enable.auto.commit=false, isolation.level=read_committed. Producer: a transactional.id unique per pod, for example enricher-<pod name>. If the pods are a StatefulSet the name also survives a restart, so the restarted pod aborts its predecessor's open transaction; otherwise the coordinator aborts it after transaction.timeout.ms (60 s by default).

producer.initTransactions();
consumer.subscribe(List.of("orders-raw"));
while (running) {
  ConsumerRecords<String,String> recs = consumer.poll(Duration.ofMillis(500));
  if (recs.isEmpty()) continue;
  try {
    producer.beginTransaction();
    Map<TopicPartition,OffsetAndMetadata> offs = new HashMap<>();
    for (ConsumerRecord<String,String> r : recs) {
      producer.send(new ProducerRecord<>("orders-enriched", r.key(), enrich(r.value())));
      offs.put(new TopicPartition(r.topic(), r.partition()), new OffsetAndMetadata(r.offset() + 1));
    }
    producer.sendOffsetsToTransaction(offs, consumer.groupMetadata());
    producer.commitTransaction();
  } catch (ProducerFencedException e) {
    producer.close(); throw e;            // another instance owns the id: stop
  } catch (KafkaException e) {
    producer.abortTransaction();
    Map<TopicPartition,OffsetAndMetadata> c = consumer.committed(recs.partitions());
    for (TopicPartition tp : recs.partitions())   // rewind what the aborted transaction read
      consumer.seek(tp, c.get(tp) != null ? c.get(tp).offset() : recs.records(tp).get(0).offset());
  }
}

No consumer.commitSync(): the offsets commit with the transaction. Billing must read orders-enriched with isolation.level=read_committed; with the default read_uncommitted it still sees records of aborted transactions.

Use only the Admin client; it reads group state without joining the group.

try (Admin admin = Admin.create(props)) {
  ConsumerGroupDescription d;
  try {
    d = admin.describeConsumerGroups(List.of(group)).describedGroups().get(group).get();
  } catch (ExecutionException e) {
    if (e.getCause() instanceof GroupIdNotFoundException) { System.err.println("group " + group + " not found"); System.exit(2); }
    throw e;
  }
  Map<TopicPartition, MemberDescription> owner = new HashMap<>();
  d.members().forEach(m -> m.assignment().topicPartitions().forEach(tp -> owner.put(tp, m)));
  Map<TopicPartition, OffsetAndMetadata> committed = new HashMap<>(admin.listConsumerGroupOffsets(
      Map.of(group, new ListConsumerGroupOffsetsSpec())).partitionsToOffsetAndMetadata(group).get());
  owner.keySet().forEach(tp -> committed.putIfAbsent(tp, null));   // owned, nothing committed yet
  Map<TopicPartition, OffsetSpec> req = new HashMap<>();
  committed.keySet().forEach(tp -> req.put(tp, OffsetSpec.latest()));
  Map<TopicPartition, ListOffsetsResult.ListOffsetsResultInfo> end = admin.listOffsets(req).all().get();
  for (TopicPartition tp : committed.keySet()) {
    OffsetAndMetadata c = committed.get(tp);
    long e = end.get(tp).offset();
    String lag = c == null ? "-" : Long.toString(e - c.offset());
    MemberDescription m = owner.get(tp);
    System.out.printf("%s %d %s %d %s %s %s%n", tp.topic(), tp.partition(), c == null ? "-" : c.offset(), e, lag,
        m == null ? "-" : m.clientId(), m == null ? "-" : m.host());
  }
}

Since Kafka 4.0, describeConsumerGroups throws GroupIdNotFoundException for an unknown group instead of returning a DEAD description. The principal needs Describe on the group (OffsetFetch, DescribeGroups, ConsumerGroupDescribe) and Describe on the topics (OffsetFetch, ListOffsets); nothing else.
